cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "lockin-validate: offline validation of quantitative investment strategies and their backtests"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Joaquín"
    family-names: "Domínguez"
  - given-names: "Mateo"
    family-names: "Domínguez"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-28"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - backtest
  - validation
  - deflated sharpe ratio
  - probability of backtest overfitting
  - look-ahead bias
  - reconciliation
abstract: >-
  An offline Python toolkit that audits the inputs of a quantitative strategy, reconstructs and reconciles its results
  from trades, detects look-ahead, omitted costs, metric errors and rule-versus-implementation mismatches, and assesses
  statistical significance and overfitting, producing a reproducible report in which every finding links to its
  evidence.
